{
  "id": "safety_valves_in_gas_and_vapor_systems",
  "title": "Safety Valves in Gas and Vapor Systems",
  "description": "Calculate the minimum discharge area of relief safety valves in gas or vapor systems using either flow rate in lb/hr or SCFM, accounting for temperature, pressure, gas properties, and system coefficients.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Safety Valves in Gas and Vapor Systems\n\nCalculate the minimum discharge area of a relief safety valve in a gas or vapor system.\n\n### Calculation Methods:\n\n**Method 1 - Flow in lb/hr:**\n- Formula: A = m T^(1/2) / (C kd kbp P M^(1/2))\n\n**Method 2 - Flow in SCFM:**\n- Formula: A = qs (SG T)^(1/2) / (1.175 C kd kbp P)\n\n### Common Coefficients (C) by Gas:\nAir: 356, Nitrogen: 356, Oxygen: 356, Natural Gas: 344, Propane: 330, Ammonia: 347, Hydrogen: 357, Methane: 348, Carbon Dioxide: 346"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "headers": [
        "Flow (lb/hr) Method",
        "Flow (SCFM) Method"
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "method",
          "label": "Calculation Method",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Flow in lb/hr",
              "value": "lbhr"
            },
            {
              "label": "Flow in SCFM",
              "value": "scfm"
            }
          ],
          "defaultValue": "lbhr"
        },
        {
          "id": "m",
          "label": "Relieving Capacity (lb/hr)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1000,
          "unit": "lb/hr"
        },
        {
          "id": "qs",
          "label": "Relieving Capacity (SCFM)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 100,
          "unit": "SCFM"
        },
        {
          "id": "T_temp",
          "label": "Temperature",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 70,
          "unit": "°F"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "label": "Coefficient (C)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 356,
          "unit": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "kd",
          "label": "Discharge Coefficient (kd)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.975,
          "unit": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "kbp",
          "label": "Back Pressure Coefficient (kbp)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1,
          "unit": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "set_pressure",
          "label": "Set Pressure (psig)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 100,
          "unit": "psig"
        },
        {
          "id": "over_pressure",
          "label": "Over Pressure (psig)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10,
          "unit": "psig"
        },
        {
          "id": "M",
          "label": "Molecular Weight (lb/lbmol)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 28.97,
          "unit": "lb/lbmol"
        },
        {
          "id": "SG",
          "label": "Specific Gravity (relative to air)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1,
          "unit": ""
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "T_absolute",
          "label": "Absolute Temperature",
          "formula": "inputs.T_temp + 460",
          "unit": "°R"
        },
        {
          "id": "P_relief",
          "label": "Relieving Pressure",
          "formula": "inputs.set_pressure + inputs.over_pressure + 14.7",
          "unit": "psia"
        },
        {
          "id": "A_lbhr",
          "label": "Minimum Discharge Area (lb/hr method)",
          "formula": "inputs.m * Math.sqrt(inputs.T_absolute) / (inputs.C * inputs.kd * inputs.kbp * (inputs.set_pressure + inputs.over_pressure + 14.7) * Math.sqrt(inputs.M))",
          "unit": "in²",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "A_scfm",
          "label": "Minimum Discharge Area (SCFM method)",
          "formula": "inputs.qs * Math.sqrt(inputs.SG * (inputs.T_temp + 460)) / (1.175 * inputs.C * inputs.kd * inputs.kbp * (inputs.set_pressure + inputs.over_pressure + 14.7))",
          "unit": "in²",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
